  "preamble": "Raising the open nucleus of [ai] to mid [e] gives [ei], the glide pulling the first element upward. The Proto-Germanic diphthong *ai became ei in Old Norse and, outside a few consonantal environments, in Old High German. In Galician-Portuguese a Vulgar Latin [ai] created by metathesis of yod (-ārius > *-airu) became ei, giving the productive suffix -eiro.",
